// ═══ RACE CONDITION: wrong result, program continues ═══
int balance = 100000;
// Thread-1: balance -= 60000; → reads 100000, writes 40000
// Thread-2: balance -= 60000; → reads 100000, writes 40000 (or -20000)
// Program CONTINUES but balance is WRONG!
// Symptoms: silent data corruption, intermittent, hard to reproduce

// ═══ DEADLOCK: no result, program freezes ═══
// Thread-1: lock(A) → wait for B (held by Thread-2)
// Thread-2: lock(B) → wait for A (held by Thread-1)
// Program FROZEN. No progress. Both threads stuck FOREVER.
// Symptoms: thread pool exhaustion, timeouts, service unresponsive

// ═══ COMPARISON TABLE ═══
// Feature         Race Condition                Deadlock
// Symptom         Wrong data / lost updates      Program freeze
// Program runs?   YES (with wrong results)       NO (stuck forever)
// Deterministic?  NO (timing-dependent)          YES (once triggered)
// Detection       Hard (intermittent bugs)        Easy (jstack, ThreadMXBean)
// Cause           Missing synchronization         Circular lock dependency
// Fix             Add sync / Atomic / volatile    Lock ordering / tryLock
// Danger          HIGHER (silent corruption)      LOWER (visible freeze)

// ═══ CAN HAVE BOTH? ═══
// YES! Fixing a race condition by adding locks can INTRODUCE a deadlock
// if locks are acquired in inconsistent order.
// Balance: enough sync to prevent races, ordered locks to prevent deadlocks.

// ═══ LIVELOCK (bonus): similar to deadlock but threads ARE running ═══
// Thread-1: try lock A → try lock B → fail → release A → retry
// Thread-2: try lock B → try lock A → fail → release B → retry
// Both keep retrying forever — running but making NO progress!
// Fix: add random backoff (Thread.sleep(random))
